    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner response, following the project's OfficeFloor + MapStruct patterns already used for sibling derived fields like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, and `ageBand`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, seed-independent derivation class in the `rest/function/owner` package, mirroring the style of `MembershipLevel`/`Locality`. It computes `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n   - `TIER` = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD`\n   - `AREA` = `METRO` when locality is `NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`, else `REGIONAL`\n   - `of(Owner)` reuses the existing `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` (including its household cap) and `Locality.of(...)` logic.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` wiring the mapper to `OwnerSegment.of(owner)`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the `ownerSegment` read-only string field so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it, with the spec description matching the requirement.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run is `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
